From 151960f95591d3a0c95b0aaa50eeb5e535bf9544 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wouter van Lent <woutervanlent@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 10:15:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] autoscroll: announce scrolling once per page, as the
 comment already claimed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 'Scrolling down by N pixels' message is yielded from inside the scroll
loop, which turns every 75ms, and the segments===1 branch it sits in holds for
the whole scroll of any page that does not grow. So a page announced itself
~13 times a second: one production crawl of a 1.500-page site logged 5.600
identical lines, which is most of that log.

The comment on the branch has always said 'only print this the first time';
this adds the flag that makes it so, for both scrollDown and scrollUp. No
change to scrolling itself — same pages, same captures, 86 lines to 1 on a
scrolling fixture.
---
 package-lock.json | 13975 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/autoscroll.ts |    32 +-
 2 files changed, 13998 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 package-lock.json

